    ds² = -(1 - r_s/r)c²dt² + (1 - r_s/r)⁻¹dr² + r²dΩ²

    where r_s = 2GM/c² is Schwarzschild radius (event horizon)

Schwarzschild Radius:
    r_s = 2GM/c² ≈ 3 km × (M/M_☉)

    For Earth: r_s ≈ 9 mm  (Earth would need to be compressed to < 1 cm!)
